  "description": "KUVKET crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H136 Co2 Gd4 N4 O29,C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.382-5.074 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.25-146.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H139Co2Gd4N5O29. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II).",
